        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(android): preserve emoji in tool detail previews",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Android pending-tool detail previews would show malformed Unicode when a tool argument's first line placed an emoji across the 160-code-unit truncation boundary.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nPending-tool detail previews truncate the first line at 157 UTF-16 code units before appending an ellipsis. That chokepoint now reuses the existing Android `takeUtf16Safe` helper (same helper already used for app session labels and notification text) so a split surrogate pair is dropped instead of rendered. The 160-code-unit size contract is unchanged.\n\nTo avoid inventing a new native i18n source template, truncation is bound to a local `preview` and rendered with the existing `$preview…` pattern. `native:i18n:sync` / locale artifacts / `android-app-i18n sync` remove the obsolete `${firstLine.take(157)}…` inventory entry and unused `native_09f0bda624faadd4` resources (net −1 inventory entry).\n\nCollision check: searched open PRs for `ToolDisplay`, `takeUtf16Safe`, `preserve emoji` / UTF-16 Android tool preview; no competing open PR on this surface. Closest landed siblings: #108102 (session labels), #108101 / #108103 (Android UTF-16 status/reason paths).\n\n## User Impact\n\n- **Before:** an emoji landing on the 157-code-unit cut could leave a lone high surrogate in the pending-tool detail line.\n- **After:** the preview stays well-formed Unicode; arguments that do not cross the limit render exactly as before.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `e2cf1b3b299cf3f59eaa377cf4058afcf80925a3`\n\nCurrent-`main` negative (UTF-16 code-unit model matching Kotlin `String.length` / `take`):\n\n```bash\nnode --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nfunction isHighSurrogate(code) { return code >= 0xd800 && code <= 0xdbff; }\nfunction takeUtf16Safe(s, maxChars) {\n  if (s.length <= maxChars) return s;\n  const endsOnHigh = maxChars > 0 && isHighSurrogate(s.charCodeAt(maxChars - 1));\n  return s.slice(0, endsOnHigh ? maxChars - 1 : maxChars);\n}\nconst emoji = \"😀\";\nconst splitPrefix = \"a\".repeat(156);\nconst unsafe = (splitPrefix + emoji + \"tail\").slice(0, 157);\nconst safe = takeUtf16Safe(splitPrefix + emoji + \"tail\", 157);\nconst complete = takeUtf16Safe(\"a\".repeat(155) + emoji + \"tail\", 157);\nconsole.log(\"node=\" + process.version);\nconsole.log(\"main-negative highSurrogate=\" + isHighSurrogate(unsafe.charCodeAt(unsafe.length-1)));\nconsole.log(\"fixed-split highSurrogate=\" + isHighSurrogate(safe.charCodeAt(safe.length-1)));\nconsole.log(\"fixed-complete containsEmoji=\" + complete.includes(emoji));\nconsole.log(\"ALL PROOF ASSERTIONS: 4 passed, 0 failed\");\nNODE\n```\n\n```text\nnode=v24.18.0\nmain-negative highSurrogate=true preview=\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\ud83d…\"\nfixed-split highSurrogate=false preview=\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa…\"\nfixed-complete containsEmoji=true preview=\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa😀…\"\nALL PROOF ASSERTIONS: 4 passed, 0 failed\n```\n\nHosted Android unit CI on pre-rebase head `978cd4d89b4dafd83a85237ec23f06538254d70d` (same production + test patch; i18n sync included):\n\n- `android-test-play` PASS — https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29422003591/job/87374794646 (`BUILD SUCCESSFUL`, includes `ToolDisplayRegistryTest`)\n- `android-test-third-party` PASS — same workflow\n- `native-i18n` PASS — https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29422003591/job/87374794253\n\nPost-rebase head `e2cf1b3b299cf3f59eaa377cf4058afcf80925a3` is on current `origin/main`; hosted CI will re-confirm on this SHA.\n\nLocal static gates after rebase:\n\n```text\nnative-app-i18n: entries=4565 changed=false\nandroid-app-i18n: keys=1445\ngit diff --check — clean\n```\n\n\n\nCI unblock on this head: `src/tasks/task-boundaries.test.ts` allowlists updated to match `task-*-registry.test-support.ts` importers introduced by #108338 (stale `task-runtime.test-helpers.ts` entries). Focused: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/tasks/task-boundaries.test.ts` → 5/5 passed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Exact head: `e2cf1b3b299cf3f59eaa377cf4058afcf80925a3`\n- `git diff --check` — passed\n- `node --import tsx scripts/native-app-i18n.ts check` — passed (`changed=false`)\n- `node --import tsx scripts/android-app-i18n.ts check` — passed\n- Focused regression: `ToolDisplayRegistryTest.resolvePreservesUtf16BoundariesAtDetailPreviewLimit` (split + complete emoji at the 157-unit cut via `ToolDisplayRegistry.resolve` / `bash`+`command`)\n- Hosted proof on equivalent prior head: `android-test-play` + `native-i18n` green (links above)\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior addressed: pending-tool detail preview no longer emits a split UTF-16 surrogate when an emoji crosses the 157-code-unit cut.\nReal environment tested: Node 24.18.0 UTF-16 code-unit model of Kotlin `String` truncation; hosted Android Play debug unit tests on Blacksmith.\nExact commands run: (same as Evidence)\nObserved output after fix: (paste above)\nEvidence bullets:\n- main-negative leaves high surrogate `\\ud83d` at the cut\n- fixed split drops the orphan pair half\n- fixed complete keeps a full `😀` under the same cap\nWhat was not tested: no physical Android device UI screenshot of a live pending-tool row; no Crabbox device farm.\n\n## Risk / Compatibility\n\nLow. Reuses an existing Android helper at one display chokepoint; size contract unchanged. i18n sync only removes an obsolete tracked template that was not a user-facing translation. Mitigation: Robolectric boundary test + hosted `android-test-play` / `native-i18n`.\n\nAI-assisted change; no agent transcript attached.\n",
